WEBVTT

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.416
what we're seeing is
that there's a network of Africans

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.056
all across the continent

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:08.256
who are rising up and fighting back
and demanding climate justice.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.360
(Applause)

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.056
MB: So Alicia,

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.856
you've said that when
black people are free,

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.816
everyone is free.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.536
Can you talk about what that means?

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.776
Alicia Garza: Sure.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.736
So I think race and racism
is probably the most studied

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.656
social, economic and political
phenomenon in this country,

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.816
but it's also the least understood.